title The ring the refusals crossed -- the Sound card refreshed, and LOCA quest two opens GREEN
prompt Keaton asked the Sound loop script updated to serve this desktop recursion session best, then run, with thanks to everyone, the baton, prin, and recur.
think The card refresh carries what tonight actually taught: a LANE'S LIVING LADDER block giving a fresh session its coordinates (LOCA, quest one closed, quest two open, the seam as the one cast with %335's optional lesson), and a ONE INDEX ONE WRITER block naming the habit the fleet's two collisions paid for -- stage only at the moment of commit, never leave work staged or unlanded between laps, touch no shelf row you did not write. The seated word choices ride in the standing-laws paragraph by rule name.
think Recur meant the next lap, and quest two rung one was pure: brushstroke/skate_event_ring.rye ports EventRing.swift bound for bound -- 128 seats, monotonic u64 head and tail, modulo only for the physical seat, refusal before mutation at both walls -- with SurfEventRing and SkateEventRing as compile-time aliases of the one type per alias-sameness.
obs The witness mirrors the five Swift tests case for case and every refusal is followed by whole-state assertions: full refuses as Full with counters, count, and the oldest event standing; the wrap keeps linear FIFO with head=96 tail=224 at refill; advanced refuses CounterExhausted at the u64 ceiling; exhaustion at init_at(max-1) refuses without touching the would-be seat; and the aliases prove type-equal at comptime. GREEN on the first run under rye run, no emitted binary, so the own-build ratchet gains no pair.
obs Thanks went to grain-d4 by name -- the Mandate builds, the clock guard, and the grace through two index collisions -- with the refreshed card offered to every seat.
loom witness=skate_event_ring capacity=128 wrap_head=96 wrap_tail=224 refusals=4 aliases_proven=comptime
